  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tuvalu Coastal Adaptation Project, Phase 3 (TCAP IB)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the Tuvalu Coastal Adaptation Project, Phase 3 (TCAP 1B), is to focus on reducing the vulnerability of the norther lagoon shoreline of Fogafale Island in Tuvalu to the adverse impacts of wave overtopping, shoreline erosion, and rising sea levels. This project builds upon the achievements of the Green Climate Fund (GCF)-)-supported Tuvalu Coastal Adaptation Project (TCAP) and the follow up DFAT and MFAT funded TCAP 1A aims to expand the reclaimed area by an additional 7 hectares,</narrative>
  </description>
